WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:09.046
Hi, and welcome to the first Crypto Nordic newsletter,
with the Nordic crypto news that mattered from the 27th of

00:00:09.046 --> 00:00:11.828
September to the 2nd of October 2026.

00:00:11.828 --> 00:00:20.141
Crypto Nordic gathers crypto, bitcoin and blockchain news
from Norway, Sweden, Denmark, Finland and Iceland, with a

00:00:20.141 --> 00:00:22.310
link to every original source.

00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:29.454
It's made with the help of AI: a bot drafts the summaries,
and they're edited for accuracy before anything is

00:00:29.454 --> 00:00:30.109
published.

00:00:30.109 --> 00:00:33.234
This narration is an AI voice, too.

00:00:33.234 --> 00:00:35.695
You may have known us as Nordic Crypto.

00:00:35.695 --> 00:00:37.375
Only the name has changed.

00:00:38.786 --> 00:00:46.050
First, from Realtid in Sweden, on the first of October:
Binance is under investigation for allegedly offering

00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:52.382
services in Europe without the licence required under the
EU's new crypto rules, known as MiCA.

00:00:53.790 --> 00:01:01.579
Dagens PS, also in Sweden, reports that Binance said it
would leave Europe, but customers are still trading.

00:01:01.579 --> 00:01:04.925
EU financial authorities now want to know how.

00:01:06.346 --> 00:01:13.188
Realtid writes that Sweden's financial watchdog sees
crypto-assets and illegal financial networks as the

00:01:13.188 --> 00:01:17.793
biggest risk of Iran and North Korea dodging sanctions
through Sweden.

00:01:19.214 --> 00:01:26.129
And Finansinspektionen's own new risk assessment finds
that weapons of mass destruction are most likely to be

00:01:26.129 --> 00:01:30.062
financed through illegal financial activity and
crypto-assets.

00:01:31.482 --> 00:01:38.770
In Norway, Aftenposten reports that three Norwegians and a
Swede have been charged in a large drug case involving

00:01:38.770 --> 00:01:42.317
drug sales on the dark web, paid for in cryptocurrency.

00:01:43.726 --> 00:01:50.704
Sydsvenskan reports that three teenagers have been
arrested in Lund, suspected of tying up a local man with

00:01:50.704 --> 00:01:52.725
duct tape to rob him of crypto.

00:01:54.146 --> 00:02:02.201
In business news, Kaupr reports that GreenMerc is cutting
costs by 4.8 million Swedish kronor a year while

00:02:02.201 --> 00:02:04.252
Northcrypto turns a profit.

00:02:04.252 --> 00:02:05.737
Kaupr is a sponsor.

00:02:07.158 --> 00:02:14.239
Norway's Finansavisen writes that Joakim Hannisdahl's new
crypto fund, built on a model that did well in

00:02:14.239 --> 00:02:18.189
backtesting, is up 39 percent since it launched in August.

00:02:19.594 --> 00:02:27.503
And from Yle in Finland: at a Finnish crypto event,
investors said community and technology are what draw them

00:02:27.503 --> 00:02:30.091
to crypto, as bitcoin rallied again.

00:02:31.502 --> 00:02:38.054
Coming up: on the 8th of October, Göteborg Bitcoin Meetup
number 49 in Gothenburg.

00:02:38.054 --> 00:02:44.186
On the 14th, Crypto killer apps at Polyteknisk Forening in
Oslo, with paid entry.

00:02:44.186 --> 00:02:47.168
On the 15th, the Uppsala Bitcoin Meetup.

00:02:47.168 --> 00:02:52.090
And on the 28th of October, Oslo Blockchain Meetup, on
Nexa.

00:02:52.090 --> 00:03:00.039
A disclosure: Jørgen, who runs Crypto Nordic, is the
speaker, runs this meetup, and works on Nexa at Bitcoin

00:03:00.039 --> 00:03:00.775
Unlimited.

00:03:00.775 --> 00:03:02.559
Kaupr sponsors the meetup.

00:03:02.559 --> 00:03:08.158
More events, including Stockholm and Helsinki in November,
are in the calendar.

00:03:09.570 --> 00:03:11.317
That's it for issue number one.

00:03:11.317 --> 00:03:18.463
All the stories, the events calendar and a who's who of
Nordic crypto are on the Crypto Nordic website, and you

00:03:18.463 --> 00:03:25.479
can subscribe to the newsletter at cryptonordic dot
substack dot com. Disclosure: Kaupr, kaupr dot io, is one

00:03:25.479 --> 00:03:27.411
of the news sources we follow.

00:03:27.411 --> 00:03:33.856
It sponsors some events in our calendar and also sponsors
Oslo Blockchain Meetup, which Jørgen runs.

00:03:33.856 --> 00:03:37.228
I work on the Nexa blockchain at Bitcoin Unlimited.

00:03:37.228 --> 00:03:39.611
Nothing here is investment advice.

00:03:39.611 --> 00:03:41.265
Made with the help of AI.

00:03:41.265 --> 00:03:42.554
Until next week!
